# cross-lib-decision — Lib A (the referring policy library).
library "Root".

// Root's decision DELEGATES to the sibling Shared library's decision via the
// cross-library qualified ref `use decision "Shared"."Sub Triage"` — with NO
// explicit `include "Shared"`. The cross-lib `use decision` alone must pull
// Shared into BOTH the CQL emit closure (`cqlByLibrary`) AND the FHIR emit
// closure (#196). It resolves to Shared's Decision PlanDefinition (policy-id-
// scoped), and the CQL-closure fix emits Shared's CQL so its FHIR Library no
// longer dangles at Inv 4 — WITHOUT the author needing a `redundant-local-include`.

concept "Active Crohns Disease":
- type is Condition.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `active-crohns-disease`.
- definition is exists this.

decision "Triage Crohns":
- when "Active Crohns Disease" then use decision "Shared"."Sub Triage".
